1081
00:44:09.940 --> 00:44:10.080
Yeah.

1082
00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:10.680
For example.

1083
00:44:10.980 --> 00:44:14.520
And the props team will come up during the rehearsal of the scene.

1084
00:44:14.520 --> 00:44:19.940
Then on the day, we're lighting, we're getting ready to shoot, and they show the actor three

1085
00:44:19.940 --> 00:44:21.340
briefcase options.

1086
00:44:21.540 --> 00:44:21.780
Mm-hmm.

1087
00:44:21.980 --> 00:44:25.000
And then the actor says, oh, no, no.

1088
00:44:25.060 --> 00:44:28.240
I imagined it would be like a distressed leather.

1089
00:44:28.520 --> 00:44:31.760
Maybe it was my father's that they passed down to me.

1090
00:44:32.140 --> 00:44:37.240
And the props person, you just see them just having a heart attack, basically.

1091
00:44:37.240 --> 00:44:42.040
And I feel like the actor and director's producers, the writer of the episode, they might all have

1092
00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:44.060
a thought last minute like that.

1093
00:44:44.160 --> 00:44:46.220
On what this prop should look like.

1094
00:44:46.520 --> 00:44:51.280
And the props person is like, always, without fail, they're always like, oh, yeah, yeah,

1095
00:44:51.460 --> 00:44:51.660
okay.

1096
00:44:52.020 --> 00:44:52.640
No problem.

1097
00:44:53.000 --> 00:44:53.720
We'll get that.

1098
00:44:53.880 --> 00:45:00.040
And then I know that they take like a van to some warehouse and they go through a giant

1099
00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:04.580
shelf of all these briefcases to try to find the thing that the actor talked about.

1100
00:45:04.960 --> 00:45:07.020
Or they run across the parking lot.

1101
00:45:07.020 --> 00:45:07.320
Yeah.

1102
00:45:07.760 --> 00:45:10.420
And like try to get something printed in the moment.

1103
00:45:10.820 --> 00:45:14.980
I have such a memory of Phil running across the parking lot.

1104
00:45:15.040 --> 00:45:15.360
Multiple times.

1105
00:45:15.360 --> 00:45:18.200
My only memories of Phil are that he is running.

1106
00:45:18.440 --> 00:45:20.080
Running or like fast walking and talking.

1107
00:45:20.280 --> 00:45:20.600
Hey, Phil.

1108
00:45:20.700 --> 00:45:21.180
Hey, how's it going?

1109
00:45:21.940 --> 00:45:24.000
No, I've just, I got to make a coffee mug.

1110
00:45:24.140 --> 00:45:25.840
I'm going to print out a thing and we're going to get that.

1111
00:45:25.920 --> 00:45:26.660
We're going to get that made.

1112
00:45:26.860 --> 00:45:27.060
Yep.

1113
00:45:27.480 --> 00:45:28.020
Can't wait.

1114
00:45:28.360 --> 00:45:28.500
Yeah.

1115
00:45:28.700 --> 00:45:29.540
Props are amazing.

1116
00:45:29.940 --> 00:45:31.920
Props, department, kickin' butt.

1117
00:45:32.460 --> 00:45:36.620
Well, throughout all of this, Dwight is just winding Andy up.

1118
00:45:36.620 --> 00:45:38.100
They've got that scene in the kitchen.

1119
00:45:38.760 --> 00:45:40.480
Dwight has clearly done his research.

1120
00:45:40.780 --> 00:45:41.140
Oh, yeah.

1121
00:45:41.500 --> 00:45:45.620
After that scene in the kitchen, there's a deleted scene of Andy in the parking lot going

1122
00:45:45.620 --> 00:45:46.740
