Amazing.

1169
00:48:01.380 --> 00:48:06.720
There are not any current acapella groups with those names, but I'm not sure about when we

1170
00:48:06.720 --> 00:48:07.060
filmed.

1171
00:48:07.380 --> 00:48:07.940
Aca what?

1172
00:48:08.240 --> 00:48:09.660
Aca, let me tell you.

1173
00:48:10.120 --> 00:48:15.060
Veda said that Rain was improvising quite a bit in this moment.

1174
00:48:15.240 --> 00:48:15.600
Oh.

1175
00:48:15.760 --> 00:48:18.260
Some was scripted, and then he just started going off.

1176
00:48:18.260 --> 00:48:18.980
I see.

1177
00:48:19.220 --> 00:48:19.540
Yes.

1178
00:48:19.740 --> 00:48:25.140
And also, Anthony shared that he pitched that Stanley should be the first person to come

1179
00:48:25.140 --> 00:48:29.360
out of the bathroom to kind of throw Andy off because Andy's so ready, and then Stanley

1180
00:48:29.360 --> 00:48:32.780
comes out, and he's like, and then he has to get his energy back up for Dwight.

1181
00:48:32.960 --> 00:48:34.480
I love that little moment.

1182
00:48:34.600 --> 00:48:35.180
Great detail.

1183
00:48:35.640 --> 00:48:44.060
All of this is going to lead to a delicious scene in the conference room because Andy informs

1184
00:48:44.060 --> 00:48:48.140
Dwight, guess who is conducting your interview?

1185
00:48:48.260 --> 00:48:48.780
Mm-hmm.

1186
00:48:48.940 --> 00:48:51.860
He's contacted Cornell, and he's going to do the interview.

1187
00:48:52.240 --> 00:48:52.480
Yeah.

1188
00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:54.380
And Dwight's like, bring it on.

1189
00:48:54.680 --> 00:48:56.700
I love this conference room scene so much.

1190
00:48:56.780 --> 00:48:58.320
I love it so much.

1191
00:48:58.540 --> 00:49:04.100
Dave shared that this conference room scene between Dwight and Andy was his first day of

1192
00:49:04.100 --> 00:49:04.480
filming.

1193
00:49:04.900 --> 00:49:05.340
What?

1194
00:49:05.620 --> 00:49:05.920
Yes.

1195
00:49:05.920 --> 00:49:09.080
And he loved that because it was so contained, right?

1196
00:49:09.380 --> 00:49:10.620
Oh, my gosh.

1197
00:49:10.620 --> 00:49:10.960
Yes.

1198
00:49:11.200 --> 00:49:11.480
Right?

1199
00:49:11.780 --> 00:49:14.640
And he said it was about a 10 to 11-page scene.

1200
00:49:14.780 --> 00:49:16.100
That's a huge scene.

1201
00:49:16.100 --> 00:49:20.200
Yes, a lot of people asked, was this scripted or improvised?

1202
00:49:20.200 --> 00:49:22.720
It was almost all scripted.

1203
00:49:22.820 --> 00:49:28.740
It was almost all scripted, but Veda said that they did let Rain and Ed really play around,

1204
00:49:28.900 --> 00:49:31.200
especially with the role model name pitches.

1205
00:49:31.460 --> 00:49:31.800
Mm-hmm.

1206
00:49:31.800 --> 00:49:34.480
And these guys kept laughing.

1207
00:49:34.560 --> 00:49:37.420
They were breaking so hard in this scene.

1208
00:49:37.600 --> 00:49:44.580
In the end, Dwight says his role models are Dane Cook, Jack Bauer, and Eli Whitney, but in the script,

1209
00:49:44.600 --> 00:49:45.180
they're different.

1210
00:49:45.340 --> 00:49:45.660
Mm-hmm.

1211
00:49:45.660 --> 00:49:48.780
And there's many takes of these names being different.

1212
00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:55.100
But there was one big part of this scene that was improvised, and Anthony talks about it.

1213
00:49:55.260 --> 00:49:56.060
It's so good.

1214
00:49:56.500 --> 00:50:02.300
That scene that we had in the conference room where they were, the double interview, as it were,

1215
00:50:02.480 --> 00:50:07.080
that was always like, had always been in there as a fun scene for the two of them to square off

1216
00:50:07.080 --> 00:50:08.100
at the end of that episode.

1217
00:50:08.560 --> 00:50:14.700
I do remember there was a moment where it was either Rain or Ed started pulling the table,

1218
00:50:14.700 --> 00:50:17.880
and I was just like, oh, we've got to do that more.

1219
00:50:18.280 --> 00:50:22.860
So I talked to Dave, Dave Rogers, who was directing his first episode of The Office,

1220
00:50:22.920 --> 00:50:26.600
and he's directed a thousand things since because he's freaking amazing.

1221
00:50:27.300 --> 00:50:29.760
I remember talking to him, they've got to just let him play with that table,

1222
00:50:29.860 --> 00:50:33.340
let him pull it back and forth, let him struggle with that and see what happens.

1223
00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:36.260
And I think we got, that was the only take I think we did of that,

1224
00:50:36.640 --> 00:50:41.660
where Rain just pulls it all the way to the wall and thanks him for coming.

1225
00:50:41.820 --> 00:50:45.540
It's just that whole, you know, those characters are all about conflict,

1226
00:50:45.540 --> 00:50:48.360
all about power shifts and that whole dynamic just felt,

1227
00:50:48.440 --> 00:50:51.580
it felt like the right place to end up with those characters.

1228
00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:56.020
And so that was a nice little bit of improv that we got to enhance on the day.

1229
00:50:56.940 --> 00:51:00.900
I feel like Dave must've been so excited after this first shoot day.

1230
00:51:01.080 --> 00:51:01.340
Yeah.

1231
00:51:01.480 --> 00:51:06.540
To get that table tugging moment, to get this whole scene, these guys are so good in it.

1232
00:51:06.700 --> 00:51:06.920
Yeah.

1233
00:51:07.160 --> 00:51:08.640
He had to have been fired up.

1234
00:51:08.900 --> 00:51:09.860
You would think so.

1235
00:51:10.080 --> 00:51:11.620
I mean, the biggest stuff was ahead of him,

1236
00:51:11.720 --> 00:51:14.160
