1261
00:52:10.380 --> 00:52:10.720
Yeah.

1262
00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:17.980
I was able to get in touch with Tug, by the way, and oh my gosh, I could not love this guy more.

1263
00:52:18.060 --> 00:52:21.920
I mean, we had such a fun time shooting together, and I had so much fun reminiscing with him about this.

1264
00:52:22.140 --> 00:52:29.260
He told me that the audition notice for this episode, it said it was looking for actors who were six foot one or taller,

1265
00:52:29.940 --> 00:52:35.020
preferably with brown hair, but it did not reveal that you would be playing Jim Halpert's brother.

1266
00:52:35.420 --> 00:52:35.620
Huh.

1267
00:52:35.620 --> 00:52:40.920
And when he got to the audition, he said, first of all, he's six foot five.

1268
00:52:41.180 --> 00:52:46.860
And when he got to the audition, Allison Jones said, you look like you could play John Krasinski's brother.

1269
00:52:47.320 --> 00:52:51.040
That's what she said, and he was like, oh, I'm going to be playing a helper.

1270
00:52:51.400 --> 00:52:51.620
Yeah.

1271
00:52:51.620 --> 00:52:53.040
That was his first clue.

1272
00:52:53.420 --> 00:52:59.820
He read with Allison's associate, Ben Harris, and the next day, he got a call that he'd gotten the part.

1273
00:52:59.820 --> 00:53:03.700
Well, I definitely felt like these guys look like they could be John's brothers.

1274
00:53:03.980 --> 00:53:06.780
And you know, John's brothers in real life are super tall.

1275
00:53:06.980 --> 00:53:08.100
They're like 6'8 or something.

1276
00:53:08.340 --> 00:53:09.520
They're like the tallest family.

1277
00:53:09.840 --> 00:53:11.180
Isn't John the short one?

1278
00:53:11.280 --> 00:53:11.680
Yes.

1279
00:53:12.060 --> 00:53:13.280
And John is 6'3.

1280
00:53:13.480 --> 00:53:14.680
Yeah, and he's the shorty.

1281
00:53:16.020 --> 00:53:17.140
That is so crazy.

1282
00:53:17.540 --> 00:53:21.860
Well, Tug said, here's the thing that happens when you're a really tall actor.

1283
00:53:22.360 --> 00:53:24.340
You usually have to bring your own clothes.

1284
00:53:24.640 --> 00:53:27.580
Listen, Tug, that's what happens when you're a really short actor, too.

1285
00:53:27.740 --> 00:53:28.800
Angela can relate.

1286
00:53:28.800 --> 00:53:32.600
He said that is his own suit, and those are his own shoes.

1287
00:53:32.840 --> 00:53:33.660
I believe it.

1288
00:53:33.760 --> 00:53:37.180
He's pretty sure that Blake wore his own clothes in the scene as well.

1289
00:53:37.660 --> 00:53:41.120
So you know this first scene at the restaurant, Angela, where Pam has met them early,

1290
00:53:41.280 --> 00:53:44.720
and she's pitching her idea for what the prank could be.

1291
00:53:44.920 --> 00:53:50.920
She says her ring, she put it in her little apron, she left it, she's going to throw another

1292
00:53:50.920 --> 00:53:51.920
girl under the bus.

1293
00:53:52.160 --> 00:53:54.520
This whole drama, she lost her engagement ring.

1294
00:53:54.820 --> 00:53:57.220
And they're like, oh, we have a better idea.

1295
00:53:57.220 --> 00:54:03.640
Their idea is that they're going to dog Pam about her career choice as an artiSt.

1296
00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:07.900
Yeah, and they said, let's do the same thing we did to Jim's girlfriend in high school.

1297
00:54:08.160 --> 00:54:09.600
What the heck, guys?

1298
00:54:09.740 --> 00:54:11.460
What is your pattern here?

1299
00:54:11.660 --> 00:54:16.480
Oh, our bit is we make the girls that Jim's dating feel crappy about themselves.

1300
00:54:16.660 --> 00:54:17.340
I know!

1301
00:54:17.680 --> 00:54:18.660
What the heck?

1302
00:54:18.660 --> 00:54:19.220
I know!

1303
00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:24.280
They said in the DVD commentary that they wanted Jim's brothers to be bad at pranking.

1304
00:54:24.420 --> 00:54:27.660
Like, they're like the less sophisticated prankers of the family.

1305
00:54:27.900 --> 00:54:28.000
Right.

1306
00:54:28.100 --> 00:54:29.460
Jim is better at pranking.

1307
00:54:29.580 --> 00:54:30.920
They're kind of lame at it.

1308
00:54:31.180 --> 00:54:33.780
So most of this stuff was scripted in the restaurant.

1309
00:54:33.880 --> 00:54:36.800
We did not have a lot of time, actually, to play around.

1310
00:54:37.220 --> 00:54:42.020
But Tug reminded me that we did improvise the very end of this scene.

1311
00:54:42.020 --> 00:54:47.480
And he said, Jenna, I'm pretty sure you improvised that line, so not the ring thing then.

1312
00:54:48.020 --> 00:54:51.440
And then the two of them are like, no, no, no, this is better.

1313
00:54:51.520 --> 00:54:51.960
This is better.

1314
00:54:52.120 --> 00:54:53.760
And I checked the script, and he's right.

1315
00:54:53.880 --> 00:54:56.340
The scene had actually been meant to end sooner.

1316
00:54:56.700 --> 00:54:58.960
That sounds like you in real life, by the way.

1317
00:54:59.080 --> 00:55:00.720
That sounds like something you would say.

1318
00:55:00.840 --> 00:55:01.620
Maybe so.

1319
00:55:01.780 --> 00:55:05.320
I feel like we've ordered lunch together, and I've gone back and forth about an appetizer,

1320
00:55:05.420 --> 00:55:08.060
and you've said, so not the dip then.

1321
00:55:08.220 --> 00:55:09.400
We're not doing the dip.

1322
00:55:09.480 --> 00:55:09.980
Just to clarify.

1323
00:55:11.100 --> 00:55:17.160
Well, Dave shared that you guys filmed this restaurant scene the day after Labor Day.

1324
00:55:17.400 --> 00:55:17.820
Oh.

1325
00:55:18.140 --> 00:55:19.500
Tuesday in September.

1326
00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:21.700
I thought that was a fun little detail to know.

1327
00:55:21.940 --> 00:55:26.180
And Kyle, the locations manager, said that this restaurant was called E3rd.

1328
00:55:26.380 --> 00:55:26.740
Mm-hmm.

1329
00:55:26.860 --> 00:55:29.300
And it was on the east side of downtown LA.

1330
00:55:29.300 --> 00:55:34.140
They were really trying to get this area to double as Brooklyn, where Pam was attending Pratt.

1331
00:55:34.340 --> 00:55:35.560
I think they did a good job.

1332
00:55:35.720 --> 00:55:35.880
Yeah.

1333
00:55:36.200 --> 00:55:38.360
Well, the restaurant was a steakhouse.

1334
00:55:39.740 --> 00:55:45.380
And in the next scene, where you see that we're eating, after Jim has arrived, we got

1335
00:55:45.380 --> 00:55:46.480
to just pick off the menu.

1336
00:55:46.740 --> 00:55:48.780
Oh, so you're really eating the restaurant food?

1337
00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:49.100
Yeah.

1338
00:55:49.340 --> 00:55:50.340
Oh, that's so lucky.

1339
00:55:50.520 --> 00:55:51.000
I know.

1340
00:55:51.220 --> 00:55:51.960
Oh, that's cool.

1341
00:55:52.260 --> 00:55:57.460
Well, Tug said he remembers it very clearly because it was the very first time he had to

1342
00:55:57.460 --> 00:55:58.440
eat in a scene.

1343
00:55:58.620 --> 00:56:03.600
And when they gave him the menu, he thought his character would order steak at a steakhouse.

1344
00:56:03.860 --> 00:56:07.980
And that John Krasinski said, oh, dude, you're going to regret that choice.

1345
00:56:08.280 --> 00:56:11.220
You're going to be eating cold steak for several hours.

1346
00:56:11.640 --> 00:56:13.140
And Tug was like, what do you mean?

1347
00:56:13.200 --> 00:56:14.160
I'm going to eat steak.

1348
00:56:14.160 --> 00:56:15.480
And that's what my character would eat.

1349
00:56:15.600 --> 00:56:17.260
And he said, John ordered a salad.

1350
00:56:17.480 --> 00:56:17.820
Mm-hmm.

1351
00:56:17.820 --> 00:56:19.940
And like a little protein on the side.

1352
00:56:20.100 --> 00:56:21.480
And that's what I ordered as well.

1353
00:56:22.200 --> 00:56:27.540
Well, Tug said that his concern about ordering a salad was that he didn't want any food to

1354
00:56:27.540 --> 00:56:29.520
fall on him during the scene.

1355
00:56:29.680 --> 00:56:31.540
He was like, this is the first time I'm eating and acting.

1356
00:56:31.900 --> 00:56:33.980
I think steak, I can get it on the fork.

1357
00:56:34.100 --> 00:56:35.120
I can get it in my mouth.

1358
00:56:35.300 --> 00:56:37.740
Well, steak is definitely easier to eat than salad.

1359
00:56:38.740 --> 00:56:42.860
Well, Tug pointed out to me, and I didn't notice it the first time I watched it.

1360
00:56:42.860 --> 00:56:47.600
But he said it's burned in his brain because this is the scene that was on his acting reel

1361
00:56:47.600 --> 00:56:48.560
for years and years.

1362
00:56:49.060 --> 00:56:55.160
So at 12 minutes, 25 seconds, John is struggling with this bite of salad.

1363
00:56:55.380 --> 00:56:56.140
You can see it.

1364
00:56:56.320 --> 00:56:57.100
I saw that too.

1365
00:56:57.100 --> 00:57:00.120
He's having a very hard time getting this piece of lettuce in his mouth.

1366
00:57:00.360 --> 00:57:07.920
And then if you watch closely, one leaf misses his mouth and falls into his lap, which was

1367
00:57:07.920 --> 00:57:12.740
exactly Tug's fear that if Tug had been eating salad, he would have missed his

1368
00:57:12.740 --> 00:57:13.100
mouth.

1369
00:57:13.500 --> 00:57:17.180
He was then glad he had ordered that steak and had to eat it for hours.

1370
00:57:17.440 --> 00:57:21.680
John, as I rewatched that, I thought, that's a really big, aggressive bite of lettuce.

1371
00:57:21.880 --> 00:57:23.220
Like, he really went for it.

1372
00:57:23.300 --> 00:57:23.800
He did.

1373
00:57:23.920 --> 00:57:27.120
You know, sometimes when you're eating salad in a scene, you don't realize what you've

1374
00:57:27.120 --> 00:57:29.440
got on the fork, and then you just have to commit to it.

1375
00:57:30.440 --> 00:57:32.000
And that was on Tug's reel.

1376
00:57:32.260 --> 00:57:33.880
So he watched it over and over.

1377
00:57:33.940 --> 00:57:36.140
Over and over again, he watched that piece of lettuce fall.

1378
00:57:36.860 --> 00:57:39.740
So you know their dinner starts out pretty sweet, right?

1379
00:57:39.880 --> 00:57:42.020
Jim is holding up a photo of his niece.

1380
00:57:42.020 --> 00:57:42.700
Mm-hmm.

1381
00:57:42.840 --> 00:57:43.040
Right?

1382
00:57:43.240 --> 00:57:43.440
Yeah.

1383
00:57:43.760 --> 00:57:45.680
So you feel like this is going to be nice.

1384
00:57:45.720 --> 00:57:46.620
It's pre-prank.

1385
00:57:46.740 --> 00:57:47.920
The prank hasn't started yet.

1386
00:57:47.940 --> 00:57:49.020
Prank hasn't started yet.

1387
00:57:49.260 --> 00:57:54.540
The photo that John is holding up is our set medic, Patrice King's daughter.

1388
00:57:54.840 --> 00:57:55.220
Aw.

1389
00:57:55.640 --> 00:57:56.800
Yeah, Phil shared that.

1390
00:57:56.920 --> 00:57:58.180
Phil would do that, you guys.

1391
00:57:58.720 --> 00:58:03.580
This scene also has the moment where all of us at the end of the scene give a look to

1392
00:58:03.580 --> 00:58:03.940
camera.

1393
00:58:04.340 --> 00:58:06.300
And it's such a cool moment.

1394
00:58:06.900 --> 00:58:11.320
Tug said he remembers Dave Roger giving him the direction to check in with the camera

1395
00:58:11.320 --> 00:58:12.180
throughout the scene.

1396
00:58:12.320 --> 00:58:16.260
And this was like so crazy to him because, you know, he'd never been in a project where

1397
00:58:16.260 --> 00:58:18.240
you were allowed to look down the lens like that.

1398
00:58:18.540 --> 00:58:19.920
But I love this moment.

1399
00:58:20.100 --> 00:58:22.340
I love the look that he gives to the camera.

1400
00:58:22.560 --> 00:58:26.320
And you just go around the table and we all give this little look to camera about this

1401
00:58:26.320 --> 00:58:28.640
prank that is not going well.

1402
00:58:28.860 --> 00:58:29.540
Not going well.

1403
00:58:29.820 --> 00:58:31.520
Dave talked about it a little bit.

1404
00:58:31.520 --> 00:58:35.960
But he said he wanted the brothers to look to camera to just give that subtle hint that

1405
00:58:35.960 --> 00:58:40.260
their mannerisms were similar to Jim, that they would check in like that.

1406
00:58:40.440 --> 00:58:43.840
At 8 minutes, 33 seconds, Pete gives a solo look to camera.

1407
00:58:44.440 --> 00:58:49.680
And at 12 minutes, 31 seconds, Tom gives a Jim kind of shrug to camera.

1408
00:58:49.860 --> 00:58:50.820
I loved that one.

1409
00:58:50.960 --> 00:58:52.300
I thought that was so good.

1410
00:58:52.560 --> 00:58:56.800
Well, as this prank continues, it is really getting under Pam's skin.

1411
00:58:57.000 --> 00:58:59.140
Like, she is getting very flustered.

1412
00:58:59.140 --> 00:59:05.820
I think particularly when he suggests that she pay the bill by drawing on the napkin.

1413
00:59:06.240 --> 00:59:13.800
Oh, Jenna, if you need a boost, listen to the DVD commentary because Veda said she was

1414
00:59:13.800 --> 00:59:15.420
so impressed with your performance.

1415
00:59:15.760 --> 00:59:16.120
Aw.

1416
00:59:16.400 --> 00:59:21.240
She said, you know, the way this was scripted is tough because Pam has to want to be on

1417
00:59:21.240 --> 00:59:25.900
board to be pranked, but then also start clocking like, hey, that's kind of a dig.

1418
00:59:26.080 --> 00:59:27.320
Okay, you're kind of going too far.

1419
00:59:27.320 --> 00:59:30.380
And she said, Jenna did such an amazing job.

1420
00:59:30.560 --> 00:59:31.540
It was really sweet.

1421
00:59:31.800 --> 00:59:32.960
Veda was showing you some love.

1422
00:59:33.240 --> 00:59:34.100
That's really sweet.

1423
00:59:34.300 --> 00:59:39.900
Well, it was kind of a fine line because everything that Veda said, part of the storyline was also

1424
00:59:39.900 --> 00:59:46.040
meant to further Pam's insecurity about the idea of being an artiSt.

1425
00:59:46.340 --> 00:59:46.820
Oh.

1426
00:59:46.820 --> 00:59:52.840
And, you know, because this is something that she wants, but Pam is not a person with a lot

1427
00:59:52.840 --> 00:59:55.020
of certainty all the time.

1428
00:59:55.020 --> 00:59:57.060
And this was supposed to play on that.

1429
00:59:57.620 --> 01:00:00.700
It was a lot for Pam to go to art school.

1430
01:00:00.780 --> 01:00:01.540
It really was.

1431
01:00:01.700 --> 01:00:01.940
Yeah.

1432
01:00:01.940 --> 01:00:05.560
And so, this is meant to kind of discourage her momentum.

1433
01:00:06.020 --> 01:00:07.540
Aw, that makes me sad.

1434
01:00:07.580 --> 01:00:08.020
Yeah.

1435
01:00:08.300 --> 01:00:08.900
I know.

1436
01:00:09.000 --> 01:00:09.380
I know.

1437
01:00:09.760 --> 01:00:15.040
I have to say, it was so nice reconnecting with Tug about these scenes.

1438
01:00:15.280 --> 01:00:17.400
You know, he said he's still in touch with Blake.

1439
01:00:17.480 --> 01:00:20.940
He still gets recognized for having been on the show.

1440
01:00:21.120 --> 01:00:21.340
Aw.

1441
01:00:21.340 --> 01:00:28.280
Something he told me that I thought was really special was that the day this episode aired,

1442
01:00:29.060 --> 01:00:35.400
Dave Rogers called him personally, complimented his performance, and told him,

1443
01:00:35.720 --> 01:00:40.380
hey, I wanted you to know that the bulk of the brothers' scenes made it into the episode.

1444
01:00:40.660 --> 01:00:43.360
And so, when you see it tonight, it's there.

1445
01:00:43.540 --> 01:00:44.680
That is so nice.

1446
01:00:44.840 --> 01:00:45.780
No one does that.

1447
01:00:45.920 --> 01:00:47.260
That was so nice of Dave.

1448
01:00:47.460 --> 01:00:48.700
No one does that.

1449
01:00:48.700 --> 01:00:52.360
But, and Tug said, you know, I'd done a ton of guest roles.

1450
01:00:52.520 --> 01:00:55.780
And sometimes you tell your whole family to watch it, and they watch it,

1451
01:00:55.840 --> 01:00:58.040
and your whole part has been reduced to one line.

1452
01:00:58.140 --> 01:00:58.820
All the time.

1453
01:00:58.940 --> 01:01:01.200
He said, so he was so excited.

1454
01:01:01.560 --> 01:01:05.240
He called his friends and family, and he was like, yes, yes, watch the show.

1455
01:01:05.240 --> 01:01:06.400
I'm really on it.

1456
01:01:06.660 --> 01:01:08.540
And the show was a big deal at the time.

1457
01:01:08.700 --> 01:01:12.240
This was a big deal to him and his friends and family that he had been on it.

1458
01:01:12.520 --> 01:01:15.380
So, Dave Rogers, you are a gem.

1459
01:01:15.980 --> 01:01:17.540
Tug, thank you so much.

1460
01:01:17.540 --> 01:01:21.520
I want you guys to know that you can catch him on a show called Now We're Talking.

1461
01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:24.040
It is a scripted comedy series.

1462
01:01:24.600 --> 01:01:28.620
And he co-created it, produced it, and stars in it.

1463
01:01:28.820 --> 01:01:31.780
And it was nominated for a WGA Award.

1464
01:01:32.220 --> 01:01:37.120
It's produced by LeBron James and Maverick Carter's company Spring Hill.

1465
01:01:37.320 --> 01:01:41.920
But Office fans, if you check it out, you might see some Office alums on there.

1466
01:01:42.100 --> 01:01:45.220
They've got Malcolm Barrett and Andy Buckley pop up on the show.

1467
01:01:45.780 --> 01:01:48.600
So, definitely check it out, because this guy is amazing.

1468
01:01:48.740 --> 01:01:50.160
Tug, thank you so much.

1469
01:01:50.640 --> 01:01:52.460
So, we finish out this Jim and Pam storyline.

1470
01:01:52.520 --> 01:01:54.860
They're leaving the restaurant, and the two of them are walking down the street.

1471
01:01:55.000 --> 01:01:57.120
And Pam's like, that's not exactly how I had that going.

1472
01:01:57.320 --> 01:01:58.860
Like, I had a whole different prank.

1473
01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:00.100
And she tells it to him.

1474
01:02:00.360 --> 01:02:04.600
And then, Jenna, Veda shared that you ad-libbed the end.

1475
01:02:04.600 --> 01:02:06.740
The line about him being bald?

1476
01:02:06.980 --> 01:02:10.620
You ad-libbed, how about we prank him on Thanksgiving about him being bald?

1477
01:02:10.900 --> 01:02:11.980
That was all you.

1478
01:02:12.900 --> 01:02:14.560
I was really proud of that line.

1479
01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:15.440
I thought that was funny.

1480
01:02:15.580 --> 01:02:16.580
Yeah, it was really funny.

1481
01:02:16.580 --> 01:02:18.380
So, you had some improvs in this one, lady.

1482
01:02:18.560 --> 01:02:19.100
I did.

1483
01:02:19.100 --> 01:02:20.040
I really did.

1484
01:02:20.660 --> 01:02:26.740
Now, I think we should wrap up this Michael and Holly storyline, because they've arrived

1485
01:02:26.740 --> 01:02:30.220
at Holly's charming little house in Nashua.

1486
01:02:30.220 --> 01:02:31.040
Oh, I know.

1487
01:02:31.200 --> 01:02:34.460
Anthony said in the script he wanted it to be a basement apartment.

1488
01:02:34.720 --> 01:02:35.060
Oh.

1489
01:02:35.260 --> 01:02:38.140
But he was like, but we don't really have basement apartments here.

1490
01:02:38.600 --> 01:02:42.080
So, they found this little house in Angeleno Heights.

1491
01:02:42.520 --> 01:02:42.980
Oh.

1492
01:02:43.240 --> 01:02:44.200
Isn't it so cute?

1493
01:02:44.200 --> 01:02:45.260
I thought it was so cute.

1494
01:02:45.480 --> 01:02:47.980
It brought up a lot of questions for me, though.

1495
01:02:48.140 --> 01:02:48.380
Okay.

1496
01:02:48.700 --> 01:02:54.980
If Holly was in Nashua, and she had to move her whole life and all her stuff and get rid

1497
01:02:54.980 --> 01:03:00.100
of her house slash apartment that she had been living in, and move to Scranton,

1498
01:03:00.220 --> 01:03:06.100
she was only in Scranton for, I think, like, less than two months, and now she has to move

1499
01:03:06.100 --> 01:03:08.740
all the way back, and it was kind of breaking my heart for her.

1500
01:03:09.120 --> 01:03:16.140
I was glad they picked a cute location, because I was thinking, oh, my gosh, she just left this

1501
01:03:16.140 --> 01:03:16.560
city.

1502
01:03:16.720 --> 01:03:17.040
Mm-hmm.

1503
01:03:17.220 --> 01:03:22.440
But then I thought it tracks that she would know where to get a cute place if she was from

1504
01:03:22.440 --> 01:03:22.700
there.

1505
01:03:22.860 --> 01:03:23.120
Right.

1506
01:03:23.640 --> 01:03:25.440
Maybe it's even her old place.

1507
01:03:25.900 --> 01:03:26.720
Maybe it is.

1508
01:03:26.780 --> 01:03:27.680
It's super cute.

1509
01:03:27.780 --> 01:03:28.440
Super cute.

1510
01:03:28.440 --> 01:03:33.860
Also, per Dave, they were really stressed about losing light, and they were going to

1511
01:03:33.860 --> 01:03:39.100
be losing some of the crew because they were going to leave to go film the Jim and

1512
01:03:39.100 --> 01:03:42.000
Pam proposal scene with Ken Kwapis.

1513
01:03:42.380 --> 01:03:42.600
Yeah.

1514
01:03:42.920 --> 01:03:45.140
So, we would do this sometimes.

1515
01:03:45.960 --> 01:03:51.360
We filmed the Jim-Pam proposal during this episode's week of filming.

1516
01:03:51.620 --> 01:03:53.080
Right, because they had to build the whole thing.

